// modeThemeName — wire key -> the `[data-mode]` theme name a surface should wear.
//
// WHY THESE ARE TWO DIFFERENT VOCABULARIES. `src/ui/theme/tokens.css` defines
// `--u37-mode-accent` per `[data-mode="..."]`, and its names are THEMES, not
// game modes: the set includes `solo-blitz` and `blitz-battle`, which are not
// mode keys at all. Passing a raw wire key straight into `data-mode` only ever
// worked because the first three keys happened to be spelled the same as three
// theme names. `daily_easy` and `daily_expert` are not, so they silently fell
// through to the `:root` default.
//
// COLOUR FOLLOWS THE TIER (David, 2026-08-27), and the tier palette is
// EASY GREEN / CHALLENGE CYAN / EXPERT GOLD (David, 2026-08-31). A mode's colour
// applies to every surface associated with it -- its stats, boards, badges and
// battles; a Daily is signalled by the timer, the once-a-day lock and the
// leaderboard, not by hue. So the map is simply the tier:
//
//   easy,      daily_easy    -> 'easy'      (green)
//   challenge, daily         -> 'challenge' (cyan)
//   expert,    daily_expert  -> 'expert'    (gold)
//
// ⚠️ NOTE WHAT DID **NOT** CHANGE. Challenge's Daily has always rendered cyan,
// and it still does -- it simply arrives there by a different route, because
// CHALLENGE moved onto the Daily's cyan rather than the Daily being pulled onto
// Challenge's violet. The store screenshots of the Daily are therefore still
// accurate. What moved is the Challenge PRACTICE round, from violet to cyan.
//
// `[data-mode="daily"]` still exists in tokens.css, and the badge showcase paints
// the Daily ARENA with it -- an arena being a ROUND spanning all three tiers.
// Nothing in the GAME routes to it any more: the badge screen sets `data-mode`
// from its own SHOWCASE_MODES table, not from here.
//
// ⚠️ IT IS VIOLET, NOT CYAN (corrected 2026-09-03). This comment claimed "the
// same cyan" and tokens.css said "deliberately still cyan" -- both described the
// INTENT of the tier-colour sweep (5541920), not what it did. That commit moved
// Challenge off violet onto cyan and, in the same edit, moved `daily` off cyan
// onto the violet Challenge had vacated. So the two rules traded values and the
// prose was never corrected. `badgeModeTokens.test.js:54` pins the violet -- it
// was updated to match the code, so no test ever contradicted the comments.
//
// Whether it SHOULD be cyan is an open product call for David: aligning the badge
// Daily arena with the tier palette repaints that tab. Do not "fix" the colour on
// the strength of these comments alone. It may also become moot -- David's
// 2026-09-03 ruling splits the badge screen into one section per Daily TIER plus
// one combined Practice, which orphans the single Daily arena entirely.

import { modeOf } from '@/game-modes';

/** The theme names tokens.css actually defines a rule for today. */
export const DEFINED_MODE_THEMES = Object.freeze([
  'easy', 'challenge', 'daily', 'expert', 'solo-blitz', 'blitz-battle',
]);

/**
 * @param {string} modeKey a wire key from the game-modes vocabulary
 * @returns {string} a `[data-mode]` theme name
 */
export function modeThemeName(modeKey) {
  // Tier IS the theme now — both rounds of a tier wear one colour.
  return modeOf(modeKey);
}

/**
 * Difficulty tier → the `var(--u37-*)` accent token.
 *
 * ⚠️ USE THIS, NOT `dailyModeAccent`, FOR A PRACTICE MODE KEY. There are two
 * exported functions named `dailyModeAccent` in this codebase and they answer
 * DIFFERENTLY for the same input:
 *
 *   leaderboard/modeAccent.js          TIER_ACCENTS[modeOf(key)]
 *   components/stats/dailyModeStats.js TIER_ACCENT[modeOf(normalizeDailyMode(key))]
 *
 * (Written without a leading "@" on purpose — inside a JSDoc block, a line that
 * starts with one is parsed as a TAG, and `@/leaderboard` made tsc report
 * "Identifier expected".)
 *
 * The second runs the key through `normalizeDailyMode`, which coerces anything
 * that is not a DAILY wire key to `LEGACY_DAILY_MODE` ('daily'). So for the
 * PRACTICE key 'expert' it returns Challenge's CYAN, not Expert's gold — correct
 * for the daily boards it was written for, silently wrong for a practice
 * surface. I reached for it while fixing PlayStartModal on 2026-09-11 and it
 * would have shipped Expert in CYAN when it should be GOLD — trading the
 * reported wrong colour (Easy's green) for a different wrong colour.
 * The sweep test caught it, which is the only reason this note exists.
 *
 * This one takes the TIER via `modeOf`, so both rounds of a tier agree and a
 * practice key answers the same as its daily sibling. `modeTheme.test.js` pins
 * it against the other maps so the three cannot drift apart.
 *
 * @param {string} modeKey any mode wire key, either round
 * @returns {string} a `var(--u37-…)` reference
 */
export function modeAccentToken(modeKey) {
  return TIER_ACCENT_TOKENS[modeOf(modeKey)];
}

/** Tier → accent token. Easy green, Challenge cyan, Expert gold (David, 2026-08-27). */
export const TIER_ACCENT_TOKENS = Object.freeze({
  easy: 'var(--u37-green)',
  challenge: 'var(--u37-cyan)',
  expert: 'var(--u37-gold)',
});
